{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: Host expression:constitutive: not induced and called guard AMPs. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (94.87%) to Ir-Def1 C=G: 15%, K: 13%. GRAVY: -0.34; mol Wt: 4497.38; mol formula: C199H300N58O48S7; mol ex coeff: 4845. Chemical modification: C5-C26, C12-C34 and C16-C36. Activity: active against Gram+ M. luteus (MIC 0.031 uM), S. aureus (MIC 1.95 uM), S. epidermidis (MIC 0.98 uM), M. maritypicum (MIC 0.98 uM) but not Gram-negative bacteria P.aeruginosa (MIC > 250 uM) and E.coli (MIC > 250 uM). SAR: DTT reduction reduced activity by 100 fold.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39193502", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Cell Infect Microbiol. 2024 Aug 13;14:1450353. doi: 10.3389/fcimb.2024.1450353. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04820", "source_id": "AP04820", "source_numeric_id": "04820", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04820", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The immune factors involved in the rapid clearance of bacteria from the midgut of the tick Ixodes ricinus.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: Host expression:constitutive: not induced and called guard AMPs. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (94.87%) to tick Persulcatusin C: 16%, G: 18%, R: 13%. GRAVY: -0.47; mol Wt: 4199.851; mol formula: C176H270N60O48S6; mol ex coeff: 3355. Chemical modification: C4-C24, C11-C32 and C15-C34. Activity: active against Gram+ M. luteus (MIC 0.008 uM), S. aureus (MIC 1.95 uM), S. epidermidis (MIC 0.98 uM), M. maritypicum (MIC 0.49 uM) but not Gram-negative bacteria P.aeruginosa (MIC > 250 uM) and E.coli (MIC > 250 uM). SAR: DTT reduction had not effect on this defensin activity.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39193502", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Cell Infect Microbiol. 2024 Aug 13;14:1450353. doi: 10.3389/fcimb.2024.1450353. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04821", "source_id": "AP04821", "source_numeric_id": "04821", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04821", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The immune factors involved in the rapid clearance of bacteria from the midgut of the tick Ixodes ricinus.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
